From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:22:51 -0643
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zumapro-tegu: Enable the AoC

Turn on Trusty, the GSA, the AoC's three mailboxes and the AoC, and give
the AoC the board's parts: the carve-out, its signed image
(aoc-tegu.bin), stock's board id and revision (0x60b02, 0x10000, from
Google's GPL tegu device trees), GNSS type 2 (the modem's integrated
receiver, as Google's zumapro-phone-ignss.dtsi), and the sensor rails,
the S2MPG15's LDO7S (1.8 V) and LDO5S (3.3 V).

Nothing starts the AoC at boot: the firmware is loaded when userspace
writes its name to the AoC's "firmware" attribute, once the modules are
loaded in order. The drivers' probes only map registers, talk to Trusty
and the GSA, and turn on the two sensor rails.

Booted on the Pixel 9a:
7.3.0-rc6-omamobile-tegu-s2mpg15-m1-g991042e2eff3-dirty with the same
nodes (the Trusty, GSA, mailbox and AoC ones enabled by overlays at
runtime, the AoC's board properties in its DT): the GSA authenticates
and starts the firmware, which reaches its 93 services and stays up,
and the sensor proxy finds the accelerometer, light, proximity and
compass sensors on the AoC.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts   | 50 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 50 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts
index b12564d63..f66e00608 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts
@@ -195,6 +195,48 @@ touch_vdd: ldo25m {
 			};
 		};
 	};
+
+	pmic-2 {
+		compatible = "samsung,s2mpg15-pmic";
+
+		regulators {
+			sensor_3v3: ldo5s {
+				regulator-name = "sensor-3v3";
+			};
+
+			sensor_1v8: ldo7s {
+				regulator-name = "sensor-1v8";
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+/*
+ * The AoC's firmware is the board's own signed image; the board id and
+ * revision are stock's for this board, and GNSS type 2 is the modem's
+ * integrated receiver.
+ */
+&aoc {
+	memory-region = <&aoc_reserved>;
+	firmware-name = "aoc-tegu.bin";
+	google,board-id = <0x60b02>;
+	google,board-rev = <0x10000>;
+	google,gnss-type = <2>;
+	sensor-1v8-supply = <&sensor_1v8>;
+	sensor-3v3-supply = <&sensor_3v3>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&aoc_mbox_a32 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&aoc_mbox_f1 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&aoc_mbox_p6 {
+	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &ap2apm_mailbox {
@@ -363,6 +405,10 @@ &gpu {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&gsa {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 /*
  * The speaker amplifiers, two TAS2572s: top at 0x48 (reset gpp6-3) and
  * bottom at 0x49 (reset gph2-1). One node each, since the tas2781 driver
@@ -634,6 +680,10 @@ &sysreg_ufs {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&trusty {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 /*
  * Bluetooth: the BCM4383 on the APM's UART at 3 Mbaud, powered through
  * BT_REG_ON (gpn8-0) behind its latch (ble-dbo on gpp24-3), with device wake
